====================================================================================
§4  The conjugation term EXACTLY: bonds get multiplied by cosh(δ log f) >= 1, diagonal untouched
====================================================================================
    max|½(A+A*) - (M - P_cosh)| (interior) = 5.684e-14   [exact identity]
    continuum form: P -> ¼|grad logW|² ;  max(P_cosh)=1.1218e-02, max(¼|grad logW|²)=2.2432e-02
    diagonal correction |diag(A)-diag(M)| : max = 5.684e-14  (exactly zero: A_ii = M_ii)
    every bond weight cosh(delta log f) >= 1 : min = 1.000000, max = 1.000102  -> hopping is strictly ENLARGED, never reduced
    => no positive zero-order term is created anywhere; the only effect is to spread the
       operator over larger hoppings, which lowers the bottom (spectral flow downward).

====================================================================================
§5  General theorem: spectrum is similarity-invariant for ANY positive invertible W
====================================================================================
    random self-adjoint M (80x80): lam_min=-2.89351291  lam_max=+9.46688165
    max |spec(S M S^-1) - spec(M)| over 6 random SPD S = 2.504e-12
    => no W of any kind (multiplicative or not) can move the bottom of the spectrum.

====================================================================================
§6  VERDICT
====================================================================================
    (a) negative-mode location      : lam_min = -g|B| (n=0, s=-1, k_3=k_4=0)  [exact]
    (b) similarity residual, worst W: 7.12e-13 -> lam_min(A)=lam_min(M)
    (c) witness <psi0|A|psi0>       : -1.125022 (max over designs; = lam_min - ¼<|grad logW|²> <= lam_min)
    (d) conjugation term            : exact lattice identity max err 5.68e-14; every bond weight >= 1.0000 (>=1, i.e. hopping only grows)
    (e) arbitrary SPD W             : spec shift 2.50e-12
    => W-CALC (pointwise cancellation of the Savvidy negative mode by a positive weight)
       DOES NOT EXIST.  Verdict (c): structural theorem. D1/W-SHIFT is a similarity.
